&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies - from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups - use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone&#39;s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Global GTM Operations team is responsible for overall productivity and effectiveness of the GTM organization, partnering closely with the sales team and teams across Stripe to drive initiatives. &amp;nbsp;This role will partner directly with the head of the global Solution Architecture, whose team is responsible for pre-sales technical assessment and technical validation of Users in partnership with Sales. This role will be expected to drive the rhythm of business, data insights / reporting, strategic initiatives, annual planning and execution. We advance the sales policies, processes and tools to drive revenue and growth.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;This is an incredible opportunity that plays an integral role in shaping and executing GTM strategies with Sales leaders. &amp;nbsp;Responsibilities include go-to-market design, resource planning, territory alignment and quotas management, sales process optimization, and business analytics. You will also partner with key cross-functional stakeholders, including Finance &amp;amp; Strategy, adjacent Sales Operations teams, Global Systems &amp;amp; Processes, and the Strategy Planning and Insights team to streamline and optimize our internal processes and deliverables (monthly business reviews, weekly forecasting calls, target setting and planning). We are looking for a self-starter who is passionate about their work, detail oriented, analytical and has demonstrated success dealing with ambiguity in a high-growth environment, and solving problems with limited oversight.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Solution Architecture team is growing rapidly and is in need of a strong strategy and ops business partner that can help scale the operations and drive strategy of the team. This entails a focus on operational projects (process design, business cadences, systems work) and everything related to planning and running their business, including: org design and planning, sales coverage models, setting SOKRs, measuring and providing insights on performance, and process improvement.&amp;nbsp; In addition to engaging with the Solutions Architecture team, you will also be collaborating with numerous cross-functional stakeholders from across the globe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Solution Architecture leadership and cross-functional stakeholders in developing go-to market strategy, resource plan and key performance metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create and manage operational processes such as territory planning, quota setting, quarterly compensation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work cross-functionally to investigate and conduct analysis on system and operational issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute initiatives designed to optimize team efficiency and productivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive rhythm of business (weekly business reviews, monthly / quarterly business reviews) with strong operational rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide insights on key performance metrics and priorities (e.g. weekly, monthly, quarterly business reviews), identify key roadblocks to progress, and work efficiently to remove them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide business analytic strength to help drive initiatives critical to ongoing growth and provide key insights for business leadership to support strategic decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive critical projects and initiatives and drive alignment with cross-functional teams across the organization by developing detailed project plans with activity based milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee implementation of enabling systems and tools, working closely with internal systems teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply. The preferred qualifications are a bonus, not a requirement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of sales strategy and operations experience in a high-tech growth environment, or operational experience in investment banking, management consulting, private equity, venture capital, or business insights / analytics roles. Knowledge of sales data such as customer accounts, opportunities and revenue. 11+ years of total work experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s Degree in a related field (e.g. Finance, Business, Engineering, Mathematics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen and ​​distinctive problem solving and analysis skills. Ability to solve complex and diverse business problems (commercial, operational, organizational).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical skills and a structured approach to solving unique business problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced SQL and Excel skills to include experience financial modelling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with large data sets, especially in analyzing large imperfect data sets to solve problems and creating scalable reports and dashboards or ad-hoc analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder management experience - with strong communication and influencing skills.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-starter and comfortable dealing with ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate clearly, proactively, and concisely&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works well under pressure, with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast-paced and frequently changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An enthusiastic &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; mentality. Works well under pressure, with a high degree of adaptability and flexibility in a fast paced, ambiguous and rapidly changing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MBA or higher degree in an analytical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior experience at a growth stage Internet/software company or FinTech&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in BI visualization tools (e.g. Tableau)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in Salesforce.com as a user and report developer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of people management experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
